/**
* @feature Print view validation – SF-424
* @specFile e2e/apply/submission/specs/sf424-submission-print-view.spec.ts
* @description Validates that SF-424 (Application for Federal Assistance) submitted data renders
*              correctly in the internal post-submission print view workflow.
*
* NOTE:
* Submitted application creates downloadable ZIP file containing PDF/XML artifacts are generated by the system.
* The validation approach in this workflow verifies the print view output instead of directly validating generated ZIP - PDF artifact.
* The print view acts as a pre-PDF rendering validation layer to confirm submitted application data is rendered correctly.
*/

Feature: Happy Path – SF-424 Application Submission and Print View Workflow
  As a grant applicant
  I want to complete the full SF-424 application submission workflow successfully
  So that I can submit a complete application and validate all submitted data in the print view

  Background:
    Given the user is able to login with all required roles
    And the system is available

  @Happy-Path
  Scenario: Complete the SF-424 Application Submission and Print View workflow for an <user type> user

    # --- Login ---
    Given the user is logged in

    # --- Navigate to Opportunity page ---
    And the user launches the URL for an opportunity with an open SF-424 competition

    # --- Starting a new Application ---
    When the user clicks "Start Application" and selects applicant type

    # --- Fill SF-424 Form ---
    And the user fills out the SF-424 (Application for Federal Assistance) form

    # --- Verify Form Status ---
    Then the SF-424 form status is marked complete

    # --- Submit Application ---
    When the user clicks "Submit application"
    Then the application is submitted successfully

    # --- Print View Validation ---
    When the user navigates to the print view URL
    Then all pre-populated fields display the correct opportunity data
    And all user-entered fields display the values that were submitted

    Examples:
      | user type    | who is applying           |
      | Organization | Organization A            |
      | Individual   | As an individual (myself) |
